/-!
# Root-marked involution geometry of the Tits group

The canonical Parrott realization gives a generator-preserving equivalence
with the derived binary Ree group. Its type-V and type-VI root representatives
are actual fixed root words. A certified conjugacy identifies the Sylow-central
r₅ with the type-V involution, completing the long-root refinement for every
nonidentity pointwise Sylow fixer.

The exhaustive automorphism table is reduced to the full binary Ree involution
coverage and proper parabolic containment for the two representatives. These
concrete premises remain open; the conditional table also takes bijectivity
of the full binary derived action. Neither odd outer order nor innerness of
all two-power automorphisms is asserted. The residual equality uses embedded
O², with parabolics defined by their actual intersections with the derived group.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith 16.1.4 and 16.1.6, printed pp.1171–1172, and the
root distinctions used in 16.5.13–14, printed pp.1201–1203; Parrott (1972),
§5, p.683; GLS3, §§2.3–2.4 and Table 2.4.
-/
